---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
const bots = [
  ['GPTBot', 'OpenAI', 'Training data for OpenAI models (GPT).', 'Blocked by default? No; opt-out via robots or OpenAI\u2019s control page.'],
  ['OAI-SearchBot', 'OpenAI', 'Search results inside ChatGPT Search.', 'Separate from GPTBot; blocking it removes you from ChatGPT answers.'],
  ['ChatGPT-User', 'OpenAI', 'Live fetches when a ChatGPT user opens your link.', 'Acting as the user\u2019s agent; usually allowed.'],
  ['ClaudeBot', 'Anthropic', 'Training + retrieval for Claude.', 'Anthropic documents both crawl and immediate-fetch use.'],
  ['Google-Extended', 'Google', 'Gemini and Vertex AI training.', 'Does NOT affect Google Search or AI Overviews.'],
  ['Googlebot', 'Google', 'Google Search indexing, feeds AI Overviews.', 'Blocking it removes you from Search itself.'],
  ['PerplexityBot', 'Perplexity', 'The Perplexity answer engine index.', 'Also respects its own publisher program.'],
  ['CCBot', 'Common Crawl', 'Open web crawl dataset used by many AI labs.', 'Legacy but still widely honored.'],
  ['Bytespider', 'ByteDance', 'Data collection behind TikTok\u2019s AI stack.', 'Reputation for ignoring robots.txt; block at WAF if needed.'],
  ['Applebot-Extended', 'Apple', 'Apple Intelligence training.', 'Distinct from Applebot (Siri/Search).'],
  ['meta-externalagent', 'Meta', 'Meta AI training.', 'Successor naming of facebookexternalhit era agents.'],
  ['Amazonbot', 'Amazon', 'Alexa and Amazon AI services.', 'Also feeds general Amazon infrastructure.'],
];

const faqSchema = {
 "@context": "https://schema.org",
 "@type": "FAQPage",
 "mainEntity": [
  {
   "@type": "Question",
   "name": "What is ai crawlers list in simple terms?",
   "acceptedAnswer": {
    "@type": "Answer",
    "text": "Think of it as the rulebook that a specific part of the internet follows. Every page in this section explains one rule, why it exists, and how to follow it correctly."
   }
  },
  {
   "@type": "Question",
   "name": "Do I need to memorize all of this?",
   "acceptedAnswer": {
    "@type": "Answer",
    "text": "No: bookmark this page and the related tools. The goal is understanding what to check and when, not memorizing syntax."
   }
  },
  {
   "@type": "Question",
   "name": "How long does it take to implement?",
   "acceptedAnswer": {
    "@type": "Answer",
    "text": "Most configurations take 5-15 minutes in your DNS panel. The verification (using our tools) takes another 2 minutes."
   }
  },
  {
   "@type": "Question",
   "name": "What happens if I get it wrong?",
   "acceptedAnswer": {
    "@type": "Answer",
    "text": "Depends on the setting: some errors cause immediate visible failures, others silently degrade deliverability or security. Every guide includes the symptoms to watch for."
   }
  },
  {
   "@type": "Question",
   "name": "Is this the same across all DNS providers?",
   "acceptedAnswer": {
    "@type": "Answer",
    "text": "The underlying protocol is identical; the dashboard layout and terminology differ. Our provider playbooks cover the exact flow for Cloudflare, GoDaddy, Namecheap, Route 53, and others."
   }
  },
  {
   "@type": "Question",
   "name": "Where can I get help if I'm stuck?",
   "acceptedAnswer": {
    "@type": "Answer",
    "text": "Each guide links to the relevant free tool so you can verify your work. The support page lists email channels for questions the guides don't cover."
   }
  }
 ]
}
---
<BaseLayout
  title="The Complete List of AI Crawlers and Bots (2026)"
  description="Every AI crawler that matters: GPTBot, ClaudeBot, Google-Extended, PerplexityBot, CCBot, Bytespider and more, with what each does and how to allow or block it."
  schema={[faqSchema]}
>
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-4xl px-4 py-12">
    <nav class="mb-4 text-sm text-ink-faint" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
      <a href="/" class="hover:text-accent">Home</a>
       <span aria-hidden="true">/</span>
      <a href="/ai-web-infrastructure/" class="hover:text-accent">AI Web Infrastructure</a>
       <span aria-hidden="true">/</span>
      <span class="text-ink-dim">AI Crawlers List</span>
    </nav>
    <h1 class="font-display text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight text-ink sm:text-4xl">The Complete List of AI Crawlers</h1>
    <p class="mt-5 text-lg leading-relaxed text-ink-dim">
      AI systems read the web through identifiable user-agents. This is the working list of the ones
      that matter in 2026: who runs them, what they feed, and the gotchas in each robots.txt rule.
    </p>

    <div class="mt-8 overflow-x-auto rounded-xl border border-line bg-panel/60">
      <table class="pdns-table">
        <thead><tr><th>Bot</th><th>Vendor</th><th>What it does</th><th>Notes</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          {bots.map(([name, vendor, purpose, note]) => (
            <tr>
              <td class="font-mono text-xs font-semibold text-accent">{name}</td>
              <td class="text-sm text-ink">{vendor}</td>
              <td class="text-sm text-ink-dim">{purpose}</td>
              <td class="text-xs text-ink-faint">{note}</td>
            </tr>
          ))}
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>

    <div class="rich-text mt-10">
      <h2>The decision, not the default</h2>
      <p>
        There is no universally correct allow/block stance. Allowing AI crawlers puts your content
        into training data and answer engines, which can mean citations and traffic, or uncompensated
        reuse depending on your business. Blocking protects content but removes you from AI answers
        as they become a discovery channel. The failure mode worth fixing is the accidental one:
        rules written years ago, or a wildcard block that quietly excludes everything.
      </p>
      <h2>See where you stand</h2>
      <p>
        Run your domain through the <a href="/ai-crawler-checker/">AI Crawler Checker</a> for a
        per-bot verdict against your live robots.txt, or the broader
        <a href="/ai-readiness-checker/">AI Readiness audit</a>.
      </p>
      
      <h2 class="font-display mt-10 text-xl font-semibold text-ink">Frequently asked questions</h2>
      <div class="mt-3 grid gap-3"><details class="group rounded-xl border border-line bg-panel/60 px-5 py-4 open:border-accent/40"><summary class="flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-4 font-semibold text-ink [&::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden">What is ai crawlers list in simple terms?<span class="text-accent transition-transform duration-200 group-open:rotate-45">+</span></summary><p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-dim">Think of it as the rulebook that a specific part of the internet follows. Every page in this section explains one rule, why it exists, and how to follow it correctly.</p></details><details class="group rounded-xl border border-line bg-panel/60 px-5 py-4 open:border-accent/40"><summary class="flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-4 font-semibold text-ink [&::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden">Do I need to memorize all of this?<span class="text-accent transition-transform duration-200 group-open:rotate-45">+</span></summary><p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-dim">No: bookmark this page and the related tools. The goal is understanding what to check and when, not memorizing syntax.</p></details><details class="group rounded-xl border border-line bg-panel/60 px-5 py-4 open:border-accent/40"><summary class="flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-4 font-semibold text-ink [&::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden">How long does it take to implement?<span class="text-accent transition-transform duration-200 group-open:rotate-45">+</span></summary><p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-dim">Most configurations take 5-15 minutes in your DNS panel. The verification (using our tools) takes another 2 minutes.</p></details><details class="group rounded-xl border border-line bg-panel/60 px-5 py-4 open:border-accent/40"><summary class="flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-4 font-semibold text-ink [&::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden">What happens if I get it wrong?<span class="text-accent transition-transform duration-200 group-open:rotate-45">+</span></summary><p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-dim">Depends on the setting: some errors cause immediate visible failures, others silently degrade deliverability or security. Every guide includes the symptoms to watch for.</p></details><details class="group rounded-xl border border-line bg-panel/60 px-5 py-4 open:border-accent/40"><summary class="flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-4 font-semibold text-ink [&::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden">Is this the same across all DNS providers?<span class="text-accent transition-transform duration-200 group-open:rotate-45">+</span></summary><p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-dim">The underlying protocol is identical; the dashboard layout and terminology differ. Our provider playbooks cover the exact flow for Cloudflare, GoDaddy, Namecheap, Route 53, and others.</p></details><details class="group rounded-xl border border-line bg-panel/60 px-5 py-4 open:border-accent/40"><summary class="flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-4 font-semibold text-ink [&::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden">Where can I get help if I'm stuck?<span class="text-accent transition-transform duration-200 group-open:rotate-45">+</span></summary><p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-dim">Each guide links to the relevant free tool so you can verify your work. The support page lists email channels for questions the guides don't cover.</p></details></div>
<h2>Related</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><a href="/how-to-block-ai-crawlers/">How to block AI crawlers</a></li>
        <li><a href="/how-to-allow-ai-crawlers/">How to allow AI crawlers</a></li>
        <li><a href="/robots-txt-guide/">robots.txt: the complete guide</a></li>
      </ul>

    <div class="mt-10 flex items-center gap-3 rounded-xl border border-line bg-panel/40 px-5 py-3">
      <span class="grid h-9 w-9 place-items-center rounded-full bg-gradient-to-br from-accent to-violet font-display text-xs font-bold text-canvas">PD</span>
      <div>
        <p class="text-sm font-medium text-ink">PromptDNS Team</p>
        <p class="text-xs text-ink-faint">Last updated: August 2026</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
